  "rationale": "The customer is an individual (Rui Baltazar Teixeira, PT nationality, DOB 1979-03-30) while the listed party is an entity (LLC BALTECH, RU address). Name similarity is 0.607, below the 0.85 threshold. No date of birth or identifiers exist for the listed party. The screener detected risk signals 'relationship_to_listed_party' (confidence 0.9) and 'sanctioned_jurisdiction_link' (confidence 0.5) in free text, both at or above the 0.5 policy threshold, and the note lacks documentary evidence (missing check reference, document number, date). Per policy, free text risk signals at or above the confidence threshold prevent closure and require escalation.",
  "what_would_change": [
    "If the customer note contained documentary evidence meeting the standard (check reference, document number, date) that resolved the risk signals, the alert could potentially be closed.",
    "If the screener risk signals were reclassified below the 0.5 confidence threshold, the free text would not block closure.",
    "If the listed party had a date of birth matching the customer's to the day and a matching nationality, true_match could be met, leading to RECOMMEND_BLOCK.",
    "If the name similarity score were at or above 0.85 and the party types aligned, the match would be stronger."
